title: 'cumulus: judge unincluded blocks by their executing runtime'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    # Description

      Fixes part of #13658

     After a V2 -> V3 runtime upgrade, the parent search judged every unincluded block by the best block's runtime, which is V3. The V2-executed upgrade block was then kept and resubmitted under V3 rules even after its relay parent had expired under V2 rules, and validators rejected the candidates.

      This PR judges each unincluded block by the runtime that executed it, its parent's:

      - V3-executed blocks need a relay parent known from the scheduling parent.
      - V2-executed blocks need a relay parent in the V2 lookahead window. An expired upgrade block is therefore dropped and rebuilt instead of resubmitted "forever".
      - V2-executed blocks never enter the V3 resubmittable segment.

      The slot-based collator also ends the slot's core loop after building a runtime upgrade.
crates:
- name: cumulus-client-consensus-aura
  bump: patch
- name: cumulus-client-consensus-common
  bump: patch
